---
description: Commit as Mark Groves and confirm GitHub author.login before pushing
alwaysApply: true
---

Before committing, set the repository git identity so Mark is both author and committer:

```bash
git config user.name "Mark Groves"
git config user.email "149283429+mark-groves@users.noreply.github.com"
```

That noreply address is the one GitHub links to user `mark-groves`. Mark must be both the author and the committer of every commit this agent creates.

A `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>` trailer is allowed. Mark stays the author.

Before pushing, verify via the GitHub commit API that `author.login` is `mark-groves`. Do not push if it is not.
